From adfdbec97fc5a4cf4a5a625253942ceb1fc31451 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 03:47:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/29] media: exynos-mfc: DPB size without S_FMT on capture,
 progressive try_fmt

A client that keeps the capture format the driver picks after the header
(GStreamer v4l2h264dec never calls S_FMT there) left raw_buf.num_planes
at 0: only S_FMT set it, so mfc_dec_calc_dpb_size() came out with a total
plane size of 0 and INIT_BUFFERS failed with
MFC_REG_ERR_INSUFFICIENT_DPB_SIZE. The 8-bit branch of
__mfc_dec_change_format() now sets it from the chosen format, as the
10-bit branches already do.

try_fmt also left field at V4L2_FIELD_ANY, which GStreamer reports as a
driver bug for every size it probes; answer V4L2_FIELD_NONE.

Signed-off-by: Artur <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/exynos/mfc/mfc_dec_v4l2.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/exynos/mfc/mfc_dec_v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/exynos/mfc/mfc_dec_v4l2.c
index f4d817caf..35c7cea22 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/exynos/mfc/mfc_dec_v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/exynos/mfc/mfc_dec_v4l2.c
@@ -262,6 +262,8 @@ static void __mfc_dec_change_format(struct mfc_ctx *ctx)
 			/* It is right format */
 			break;
 		}
+		/* only S_FMT set this before: without it the DPB size is 0 */
+		ctx->raw_buf.num_planes = ctx->dst_fmt->num_planes;
 	}
 
 	if (org_fmt != ctx->dst_fmt->fourcc)
@@ -414,6 +416,10 @@ static int mfc_dec_try_fmt(struct file *file, void *priv, struct v4l2_format *f)
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/* progressive unless the stream says otherwise (g_fmt reports that) */
+	if (pix_fmt_mp->field == V4L2_FIELD_ANY)
+		pix_fmt_mp->field = V4L2_FIELD_NONE;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
